rem Twenty-two Foolish Primes
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=239
rem Find the chance that, in a random
rem permutation of 1 to N, exactly Keep
rem of the primes are not in place
rem and the other primes stay put

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option N integer = 100
option Keep integer = 22

rem The primes that stay can be chosen
rem in C(P, P - Keep) ways. Of the rest,
rem Keep primes must all move and the
rem others are free. By inclusion and
rem exclusion on the primes that do
rem stay, that is sum (-1)^j C(Keep, j)
rem (M - j)! for M = N - P + Keep.
Pr = primes till (N + 1) array
P = Pr len
M = N - P + Keep
Fact = (1 to N array) scan * with 1
J = 0 to Keep array
Sign' = 1 - 2 * (J mod 2)
Binom' = Keep binomial J
Free' = Fact (M - J)
Moves = (Sign * Binom * Free) sum
Pick = P binomial Keep
Total = Fact N
Answer = Pick * Moves / Total round 12
Answer print
